              <zone fixed-size='305' h='76852' id='12' is-fixed='true' name='Attainment V House Prices' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.0v5aiq917qmz1o123gfz90s8aa7x].[none:DateCode (house_prices.csv):ok]' type-v2='color' w='9517' x='417' y='22407'>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10000' id='27' type-v2='text' w='89649' x='9934' y='89259'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Methodology</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Data sources:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Scottish Government house-price statistics and school-leaver attainment data, matched using 2011 Data Zone geography codes.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Study period:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> 2014–2018, covering the years available in both datasets for this analysis.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Data preparation:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> The datasets were matched by Data Zone code and year. House-price records were restricted to median prices, and attainment reporting periods were aligned to their corresponding comparison year. Records without a matching attainment value were retained for transparency but excluded where both measures were required for comparison.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Analysis:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> The scatter plot explores the relationship between average highest qualification scores and median house prices across Data Zones. Year colours and trend lines help illustrate patterns across the study period.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Limitations:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Attainment figures are based on overlapping three-year reporting periods, so adjacent years are not independent observations. Data Zone averages can conceal differences between households and individuals. Missing matches and extreme house-price values may also affect the results.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Interpretation:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> This analysis identifies area-level associations; it does not establish that higher house prices cause higher educational attainment, or vice versa.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
